  "stage": "synthesis-review",
  "summary": "Cold review, iteration 3, of the concise study (synthesis.tex, 12 physical pages). I verified the packet hash and all 15 sealed input hashes. Compared with the iteration-2 seal, only sections/concise/90-apparatus.tex and synthesis.tex changed. I rebuilt the study from the sealed sources in my scratch directory. It settles in two passes and the PDF is byte-identical to the derive-synthesis-3 proof (SHA-256 b748378f...). The aux file is unchanged (9fa9be30...), so the zref markers still put the inventory and all four sense rows on p. 1, the chronology alone on p. 2, the themes on pp. 3-4 and the commentary from p. 5. The log has no box, LaTeX or reference warnings, and all 17 fonts are embedded. I diffed the extracted text against the build-artifacts PDF and found only four changes: the title block, four References entries, the revision timestamp and one blank extraction line on p. 1. The new subtitle, 'The King's Wedding Feast: A Concise Study of Three Interpretations', is set in the upright subtitle field that guidance/liturgy/propers-three-documents.md gives to \\propertitle, and p. 1 still holds the complete 13-row map and the four sense rows. The four shortened References entries keep every locus, edition, volume, page and year. The qualifications they gave up are still in the Scope and Qualifications note: Irenaeus as a machine-read text of the printed volume (line 57), and the Mystagogical Catecheses as transmitted under Cyril's name with the editor's report of manuscripts naming John of Jerusalem (lines 68-70). 'At vatican.va' matches the existing Nova Vulgata entry, so no evidence is upgraded and no new source-dependent claim is introduced. On my rebuild, the colophon's last line on p. 12 ends at y 744.8 pt of 792, on the same page as the terminal content. The derive-synthesis-3 audit entry and its generation-metadata contribution (packet effort high, which matches the packet) describe the edits accurately. tools/check-generation-metadata passes against the source and my rebuilt PDF, and tools/check-proper-components passes the content phase and, against my aux file, the artifacts phase. Limits: I did not re-verify the unchanged components, which were sealed and reviewed at iterations 0-2, against their sources, and I judged the homily files only as far as the shared generation record. SYN-007 stays advisory in research/scope.md. Verdict: PASS."
}
